data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/report.md\", \"content\": \"# Campaign csrclinh — \\\"greet, tested\\\" — final report\\n\\n## Outcome: campaign-met\\n\\nAll three mission criteria are satisfied, independently verified against\\ndev's branch (not just dev's self-report):\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` defines `greet(name)` returning `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` covers a normal name (`greet(\\\"World\\\")`) and the\\n   empty string (`greet(\\\"\\\")`).\\n3. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` exits 0 (2 tests, OK) — confirmed\\n   by checking out dev's branch into an isolated worktree at\\n   `/tmp/verify_dev` and running the command directly, rather than trusting\\n   dev's reported output.\\n\\n## Work performed\\n\\n- Dispatched the mission requirements to `dev` verbatim (dispatch `d002`).\\n- `dev` implemented both files and committed as `ddc9896` on\\n  `cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`, on top of the shared base\\n  `1053761f6a654e7ea58deb67a671a00d2e7fc8ac`.\\n- Orchestrator fetched the branch, diffed it against base, and re-ran the\\n  exact verification command in a clean worktree. Verification matched\\n  dev's report exactly.\\n- Accepted `d002` from dev.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Orchestrator wrote no code itself (per role), so its own branch\\n  (`cs-sandbox/<ORCHESTRATOR:1>.<GROUP:1>`) has no code commits\\n  — the delivered implementation lives on dev's branch, which is the\\n  authoritative artifact for this mission.\\n- No obstacles, restarts, or lost machines occurred. One dispatch cycle was\\n  sufficient; dev's first attempt was accepted without rework.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

